=== CMD 29 driver status WITH tmc2209-softwareserial-read LIVE ===
    v = [comm, flags, current_scaling]
  read 1: dt= 0.156s  OK:{"msg":"Driver status","v":[0.00,0.00,-1.00]}
  read 2: dt= 0.159s  OK:{"msg":"Driver status","v":[0.00,0.00,-1.00]}
  read 3: dt= 0.154s  OK:{"msg":"Driver status","v":[0.00,0.00,-1.00]}
  read 4: dt= 0.155s  OK:{"msg":"Driver status","v":[0.00,0.00,-1.00]}
  read 5: dt= 0.159s  OK:{"msg":"Driver status","v":[0.00,0.00,-1.00]}

comm = 0 with the read fix live isolates the readback failure to the hardware
bridge: the 10 kOhm resistor is still on the RX side, so the Arduino's
push-pull SoftwareSerial TX idles HIGH on the shared node and the driver cannot
pull it down to reply.  It has to be A1 --1kOhm-- NODE, with A0 and PDN_UART
both directly on NODE.  See §14.7 of opentrons-pipette-wiring.md.

